    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d721">

                <pb facs="1307" n="1183" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1183"/>

                <head>No. 717.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Heap.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 27,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 32.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your dispatch No. 4, of the
                    4th instant, touching the protest of American citizens against the payment of
                    taxes upon their property, in anticipation of a forced loan by the Government of
                    Turkey, and to inform you that, in this matter, you may act in concert with the
                    representatives of the other powers at Constantinople, as proposed in your
                    dispatch.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
